    "missing": [
      {
        "what": "Llama-3.1-8B is evaluated, and the authors report 'catastrophic failure' and instruction failures compared with Llama-3.1-70B. This is the only same-family scale contrast, but no numbers are given.",
        "locator": "Sections 8.2-8.3, Table 3",
        "versions": "V6"
      },
      {
        "what": "Per-model performance across context-length bins. Larger models are said to be more resilient beyond 1500 words, while Qwen-2.5-7B drops.",
        "locator": "Figure 4, Section 8.2",
        "versions": "V6"
      }
    ],
    "verdict_notes": "The evidence is very weak for scaling laws: there are six heterogeneous models, the frontier model's size is unknown, there are no uncertainty estimates, and the overlap metrics are acknowledged to be unreliable. The reader's 'supports' label using Gemini as 'largest model' is unfounded, because Gemini's size is unstated. Tranche changed from T2 to T3 (a new downstream setting)."
  },
